NAME
       netif_get, netif_set - network interface configuration

SYNOPSIS
       #include <sys/cervus.h>

       int netif_get(int idx, cervus_netif_t *out);
       int netif_set(int idx, uint32_t ip, uint32_t mask,
                     uint32_t gw, uint32_t dns);

DESCRIPTION
       netif_get reports one interface: name, link state, MTU, hardware
       address, addresses and the packet, byte and drop counters.
       Walking the index until it fails enumerates them.

       netif_set assigns a static configuration; a zero for the gateway
       or DNS leaves that setting alone. This replaces whatever DHCP
       configured.

RETURN VALUE
       0 on success, negative when there is no such interface.

SEE ALSO
       ifconfig(1), ip(1), socket(2)
